---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../utils/path';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Software developer, AI tinkerer, and dad of twins — thinking out loud about building things and living with intention."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Hi, I'm Ben. I'm a software developer who spends a lot of his time thinking
      about AI — not just as a tool, but as something that's genuinely reshaping
      what it means to build things, to work, and to be useful. I care about that
      deeply, and I try to keep one question close in everything I make: is this
      actually making life better in a way that matters?
    </p>
    <p>
      Away from the keyboard, I'm a dad to twin boys and a husband to my wife,
      Katie. My family is the anchor and the reason behind most of what I do.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also think a lot — maybe too much. I've been told I overthink things, and
      I won't argue with that. But I'd rather be the kind of person who wrestles
      with the hard questions than one who doesn't notice them. I'm drawn to
      philosophy, to agency, and to what it means to live with intention — and I
      believe people have far more power to shape their circumstances than they
      usually give themselves credit for.
    </p>

    <h2>What I write about</h2>
    <p>Whatever's on my mind, honestly. Usually some mix of:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Building</strong> — things I'm making, and lessons learned the hard way</li>
      <li><strong>AI</strong> — where it's going, and what excites and concerns me about it</li>
      <li><strong>Ideas</strong> — philosophy and the kind of questions that don't have clean answers</li>
      <li><strong>Family &amp; life</strong> — reflections on being a dad, a husband, and a person trying to do good work</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Think of this as my public notebook — a place to scribble. No fixed cadence
      and no content calendar; just whatever's worth writing down.
    </p>

    <h2>Follow along</h2>
    <p>
      New posts go out on the <a href={href('/rss.xml')}>RSS feed</a> — drop that link
      into any reader and you'll catch them as they land. The site itself is built with
      <a href="https://astro.build" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Astro</a> and hosted
      free on GitHub Pages, so every change I make redeploys automatically.
    </p>
    <p>Thanks for being here.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
